# Copy to .env.local for local development.

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL is the OWNER connection. Used by migrations, the seed, the
# importers and the test harness — all of which legitimately need to reach
# across tenants. Postgres exempts superusers from Row-Level Security.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://mandovara:mandovara@localhost:15432/mandovara?schema=public"

# APP_DATABASE_URL is the RESTRICTED connection the running application uses.
# The role must be NOT superuser and NOT BYPASSRLS, otherwise the §3.2 RLS
# policies are silently skipped and tenant isolation is decorative.
#
# Create it once:
#   APP_DB_PASSWORD='<strong password>' node scripts/setup-app-role.mjs
#
# If unset, the app falls back to DATABASE_URL — convenient locally, but it
# means RLS is NOT enforced. Always set it in production.
APP_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://mandovara_app:mandovara_app_local@localhost:15432/mandovara?schema=public"

REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:56379"

# REQUIRED. Signs session cookies (HMAC-SHA256). Must be 32+ characters.
# Generate: `openssl rand -hex 32` (produces 64 hex chars).
# Rotating this invalidates every active session — do it if it leaks.
SESSION_SECRET=""

# Set to "false" only while serving over plain HTTP (pre-TLS). Browsers refuse
# to store Secure cookies over HTTP, so leaving it on breaks login silently.
# COOKIE_SECURE="false"

# ── e-invoicing (IRN) — OPTIONAL ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only applicable above the GST e-invoice AATO threshold (₹5 crore at time of
# writing) — confirm with the CA before enabling (CLAUDE.md §1.6).
#
# All THREE must be set or the subsystem stays off: every invoice is left at
# irnStatus NOT_REQUIRED and billing is completely unaffected. With them set,
# invoices register asynchronously and retry on GSP outage; a rejected document
# goes to FAILED and needs a human.
# GSP_BASE_URL=""
# GSP_CLIENT_ID=""
# GSP_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# ── Error monitoring — STRONGLY RECOMMENDED in production ────────────────────
# Sentry is already wired (src/instrumentation.ts, next.config.ts) and fully
# gated on the DSN: unset, it no-ops and the build proceeds. Set, you find out
# about a production failure from a report rather than from an angry phone call.
#
# SENTRY_DSN is server-side; NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN is the browser half. Set
# both — they can be the same project DSN.
# SENTRY_DSN=""
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=""

# ── Cookie security ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session cookies are marked Secure automatically when NODE_ENV=production.
# Set this to "false" ONLY when running a production build over plain HTTP on
# a LAN for testing — a Secure cookie is never sent over http:// and the login
# will appear to succeed and then bounce you straight back to the sign-in page.
# Never set it to "false" on a public deployment.
# COOKIE_SECURE="true"

# ── Bulk import endpoint — OPTIONAL ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret for the stock/catalog import route. Leave unset and the
# endpoint refuses every request, which is the correct default; set it only
# while running a migration, and rotate it afterwards.
# IMPORT_TOKEN=""
